        {
          "name": "encode",
          "path": "lucid.models.generative.vjepa2_ac._model.VJEPA2ACModel.encode",
          "kind": "function",
          "labels": [],
          "signature": "encode(video: Tensor)",
          "source": "https://github.com/lucid-official/lucid/blob/0133691/lucid/models/generative/vjepa2_ac/_model.py#L135",
          "subcategory": "model",
          "summary": "Encode every frame to its own latent grid, `(B, T * P, D)`.",
          "extended": "One action-model step is **one frame**, not one two-frame tubelet.\nThe encoder's patch embedding is three-dimensional and wants\n`tubelet_size` frames, so each frame is repeated to fill one —\nwhich is what the released code does in both its training loop\nand its energy-landscape example:\n\nc.permute(0, 2, 1, 3, 4).flatten(0, 1).unsqueeze(2).repeat(1, 1, 2, 1, 1)\n\nPairing two *distinct* frames instead would halve the temporal\nresolution and take one action per two frames, which is not the\nrate the released checkpoint was post-trained at.",
          "parameters": [],
          "returns": {
            "annotation": "Tensor",
            "description": ""
          },
          "raises": [],
