        {
          "name": "forward",
          "path": "lucid.models.generative.vjepa2_ac._model.VJEPA2ACModel.forward",
          "kind": "function",
          "labels": [],
          "signature": "forward(video: Tensor, actions: Tensor, states: Tensor, extrinsics: Tensor | None = None)",
          "source": "https://github.com/lucid-official/lucid/blob/0133691/lucid/models/generative/vjepa2_ac/_model.py#L175",
          "subcategory": "model",
          "summary": "One teacher-forced transition step over a clip.",
          "extended": "The clip's first `T - 1` frames are the context and its last\n`T - 1` are the target: the predictor is asked what the *next*\nframe looks like, which is the post-training objective.  A\nconditioning row is therefore one per transition, so `actions`,\n`states` and `extrinsics` carry `T - 1` of them.",
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "video",
              "annotation": "Tensor",
              "description": "Clip `(B, T, C, H, W)` with `T >= 2`.",
              "default": null
            },
            {
              "name": "actions",
              "annotation": "Tensor",
              "description": "`(B, T - 1, action_dim)` and `(B, T - 1, state_dim)`.",
              "default": null
            },
            {
              "name": "states",
              "annotation": "Tensor",
              "description": "`(B, T - 1, action_dim)` and `(B, T - 1, state_dim)`.",
              "default": null
            },
            {
              "name": "extrinsics",
              "annotation": "Tensor or None",
              "description": "`(B, T - 1, extrinsics_dim)` when the config enables them.",
              "default": "None"
            }
          ],
          "returns": {
            "annotation": "VJEPA2ACOutput",
            "description": "The predicted next latents, the context they came from, the\nlatents actually observed at those frames, and the L1 between\nthem."
          },
          "raises": [],
          "examples": [],
          "notes": [
            "Both sides are layer-normalised before the loss when\n`normalize_targets` is set, as the released loop does.  Comparing\na prediction against the frame it was *given* — which is what\nscoring the unshifted latents would do — is satisfied by copying\nthe input, since the predictor's attention is frame-causal."
          ],
          "attributes": [],
          "warns": [],
          "see_also": []
        }
      ],
      "summary": "V-JEPA 2-AC encoder plus action-conditioned latent predictor.",
      "extended": null,
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "config",
          "annotation": "VJEPA2ACConfig",
          "description": "Frozen model configuration.",
          "default": null
        }
      ],
      "returns": null,
      "raises": [],
      "examples": [],
      "notes": [
        "The encoder is applied independently to each frame, repeated to fill\nthe patch embedding's tubelet.  A video with `T` frames therefore\nproduces `T` action-model steps, each containing\n`(image_size // patch_size) ** 2` spatial tokens — one step per\nframe, as the released training loop and energy-landscape example\nboth do.  `forward` takes one conditioning row per *transition*,\nso `T - 1` of them.  Planning and controller search stay outside the\nmodel."
      ],
      "attributes": [],
      "warns": [],
      "see_also": []
